{
 "id": "2026-ma-street",
 "name": "Street Comfort in Zibo: Twelve Roads",
 "description": "Method replication: same task, scale, images per road and timing as the paper; the images are not the paper's stimuli (12 Baidu street views re-fetched on the same 12 roads of Zhangdian District, Zibo: Zhongrun Ave, Huaguang Rd, Renmin West Rd, Unicom Rd, Communist Youth League West Rd, Jinjing Ave, Liuquan Rd ×2, Beijing Rd ×2, Shiji Rd, West Second Rd). Each picture stays on screen for 12 s before the answer buttons appear, with a 5 s blank between pictures; participants rate the comfort of the street landscape on a 5-point Likert scale.\n\nOriginal study: Ma & Gao (2026), Sustainability 18(5), 2220. 38 landscape architecture students (18–24) viewed one Baidu street view of each of 12 roads for 12 s with a head-mounted eye tracker, then rated comfort on a 5-point scale; comfort scores were related to eye-movement metrics and segmented elements (green view, sky, building, road, advertising ratios).\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) images are newly fetched Baidu views on the same roads, not the paper's images; (2) no eye tracking, the viewing time is only enforced on screen; (3) online self-completion instead of a lab session, ratings given right after each picture; (4) the scale end labels (very uncomfortable to very comfortable) are ours, the paper only names a 5-point comfort scale; (5) three background questions were added.",
